  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Commerce obligated $94.6M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Commerce recorded 154 awards with an average award size of $614K, and obligations fell 98.1% year over year. Fiscal-year context shows prior annual obligations were $4.1B in FY22, $5B in FY23, $5.2B in FY24, $4.2B in FY25, and $5.1B in FY26. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Other Computer Related Services accounted for $63.7M of FY2027 to date obligations, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $26M and Web Search Portals and All Other Information Services at $2.9M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $60.5M in FY2027 to date, with HALVIK LLC at $9.6M and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $9.2M. The picture is one of concentrated spending in IT-related categories and a small set of large vendors receiving most dollars in the fiscal-year-to-date period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations drop so sharply year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce obligated $94.6M in FY2027 to date, and obligations fell 98.1% year over year. Prior full fiscal years show much larger totals: $4.1B in FY22, $5B in FY23, $5.2B in FY24, $4.2B in FY25, and $5.1B in FY26. The current-year total is partial (fiscal year to date), which explains why the year-over-year comparison is so large."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are FY2027 to date dollars concentrated?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services captured $63.7M of FY2027 to date obligations, and Computer Systems Design Services captured $26M. The top vendor was GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. with $60.5M, followed by HALVIK LLC with $9.6M and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC with $9.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Commerce spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Commerce obligated $94.6M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Commerce reported 154 awards and an average award size of $614K during the fiscal-year-to-date period. Prior full fiscal years were larger: $4.1B in FY22, $5B in FY23, $5.2B in FY24, $4.2B in FY25, and $5.1B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Commerce buy?",
      "a": "Commerce buys a lot of information technology and services. Other Computer Related Services accounted for $63.7M, Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $26M, and Web Search Portals and All Other Information Services accounted for $2.9M in FY2027 to date. Security Guards and Patrol Services, Facilities Support Services, and Engineering Services also appear among the top categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Commerce's largest contractors?",
      "a": "GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. was Commerce's largest contractor with $60.5M in FY2027 to date. HALVIK LLC received $9.6M and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC received $9.2M. ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC, RELX INC., and other vendors also appear in the top 10 list."
    }
